    "summary": "Alligator suite, fierce Eleven, soaring Lovelight and tight jams",
    "blurb": "The Fillmore West show erupts with a monster Alligator > Caution > Feedback jam, an incendiary The Eleven, and a luminous Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s guitar flows with ideas while Phil locks in a powerful groove; Pigpen adds swagger on the first set. The multi‑track soundboard capture offers crystal‑clear imaging and superb balance.",
    "review": "On February 28, 1969 at the Fillmore West the Dead unleashed one of their early‑period monsters. A three‑set marathon opens with Pigpen’s bluesy swagger on Good Morning Little School Girl and a ripping Turn On Your Lovelight, then dives into a cryptic second set that weaves Cryptical Envelopment into The Other One, Dark Star → Saint Stephen and builds to the thunderous Eleven before collapsing into the searing Death Don’t Have No Mercy. The third set is dominated by an all‑out Alligator suite—Alligator → Caution (Do Not Stop On Tracks) → Feedback → And We Bid You Good Night—that showcases relentless drumming, Jerry’s soaring leads and Phil’s bass ownership. Across all three soundboard recordings the performance is consistently praised as tight, inspired, and historically significant, with the multi‑track version providing the most vivid listening experience despite minor speed/pitch quirks.",
